From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 03:10:23 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 104/161] hjviewer: password-less sessions end with their key
 (TV-W5)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

TV-W5 (design build/v19/design/w5.md, decisions D-5 and D-6, critic 2-3
and S-01): the PC's service keeps a book of the sessions it let in by a
same-account proof, in memory only (src/hjviewer_account/pc/sessions.rs).
Every signed list the sync task keeps (active or disabled), a signed
revoked, and this PC's own logout (D-6, critic S-01) move the book: a
session the latest no longer lets in by the new-proof rule (entry_allows,
taken out of check_key_login) gets a mark and one log line. The book has
an epoch, read before a proof reads its list, so a proof let in by an
older list is judged again by the newest when it enters the book. An
expired list, a failed sync, a 401, an unsigned or forged answer and the
PC's [끄기] mark nothing.

The connection's existing one-second timer reads the mark
(hjv_account_cut): send_close_reason_no_retry with the Korean text and
its "not allowed" mark (login ended / password-less ended), a lock after
a remote screen session (lock_after_session_end), on_close(..., true).
The mark lives in the one proof record (HjvProven.session, critic 2-3),
set before the logon response; the book forgets a line once the
connection drops it (a Weak of the mark).

D-5: a signed disabled list (switch off, blocked account, off the
allowlist) ends the open password-less sessions. D-6: the PC's logout
(Syncer::unbind dropping the binding) ends them; [끄기] does not.

Words I-3: the Korean cell of logoutRemoteNow now says the PC's logout
ends a password-less connection (the English cell came with the words
lane).

hjv-e2e: a stream or screenshot session the PC closes with a reason
prints "hjv-e2e: closed: <reason>" and exits 6.

Tests T1-T11 of the design: judge's table, entry_allows against
check_key_login, one mark per list, the book forgetting dropped
sessions, the epoch race both ways, the sync task against the fake
hjv-api (a list without the key, failures, expiry, revoked, a new
binding with and without the key, the PC's logout and [끄기]), and the
close texts against check_if_retry and the texts.rs rules.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
